  Monks should be a good challenge.  Note that they can get to at least
basic in all spell schools.  Ranged missile weapon should be knives,
unless they get an artifact dagger as a divine gift.  Even at unskilled
the intrinsic +2 to hit, low weight, lack of disappearing, etc. makes
knives workable.  Add in enchantment for both to-hit and damage bonuses
and they'll be even better.

  Healers make great petmasters and have a lot of tricks available from
their starting equipment and food.  They can get to Skilled with
daggers.  At skilled it's d2 per firing instead of d3.  That could start
weaning you off of multi-shot missiles.  

  One thing to try with Healers is using knives as the missile weapon.
They start with basic skill in knives.  Knives weigh half as much as
daggers.  They're not multishot.  That will teach you to start throwing
even earlier.  As long as you kill the monster before it reaches you,
that's what counts.

  A knight with #jumping has a good early game.  Late game the MMoM
doubles the damage of the spell of Magic Missile (also some other
restricted spell/wand attacks.)





